     Actually,[0m[2m looking more[0m[2m carefully:[0m[2m the `[0m[2mawait[0m[2m asyncio.sleep[0m[2m(0[0m[2m.01[0m[2m)` is[0m[2m the problem[0m[2m. During[0m[2m that[0m[2m await[0m[2m, another[0m[2m task[0m[2m can run[0m[2m and see[0m[2m the same[0m[2m job as[0m[2m pending[0m[2m. We[0m[2m need to[0m[2m remove[0m[2m that[0m[2m sleep or[0m[2m ensure[0m[2m atomic[0m[2mity[0m[2m. But[0m[2m wait -[0m[2m if[0m[2m we just[0m[2m remove the[0m[2m sleep,[0m[2m there's[0m[2m still a[0m[2m race between[0m[2m the check[0m[2m `[0m[2mif job[0m[2m["status[0m[2m"] ==[0m[2m "pending[0m[2m"` and[0m[2m the assignment[0m[2m `job[0m[2m["status[0m[2m"] =[0m[2m "processing[0m[2m"`.[0m[2m In asyncio[0m[2m with[0m[2m a single[0m[2m thread[0m[2m, other[0m[2m tasks can[0m[2m only run[0m[2m at[0m[2m await points[0m[2m. So[0m[2m removing[0m[2m the await[0m[2m would make[0m[2m it atomic[0m[2m in[0m[2m the[0m[2m sense[0m[2m that[0m[2m no other[0m[2m task can[0m[2m inter[0m[2mleave[0m[2m between the[0m[2m check and[0m[2m the set[0m[2m ([0m[2msince there's[0m[2m no await[0m[2m between[0m[2m them).[0m[2m
     
     Actually[0m[2m, in[0m[2m Python asyncio[0m[2m with[0m[2m a single[0m[2m event loop[0m[2m thread[0m[2m, cooperative[0m[2m multit[0m[2masking means[0m[2m tasks[0m[2m only[0m[2m switch[0m[2m at await[0m[2m points.[0m[2m So if[0m[2m we remove[0m[2m the `[0m[2mawait asyncio[0m[2m.sleep([0m[2m0.[0m[2m01)`,[0m[2m the check[0m[2m and set[0m[2m happen[0m[2m without[0m[2m any await[0m[2m in[0m[2m between,[0m[2m making them[0m[2m effectively[0m[2m atomic.[0m[2m
     
     But wait[0m[2m,[0m[2m let[0m[2m me think[0m[2m again[0m[2m. The[0m[2m `for[0m[2m`[0m[2m loop iter[0m[2mates over[0m[2m `self[0m[2m._jobs[0m[2m.values()[0m[2m`. If[0m[2m two workers[0m[2m hit[0m[2m this[0m[2m at the[0m[2m same time[0m[2m ([0m[2mbefore[0m[2m any[0m[2m await),[0m[2m they both[0m[2m could[0m[2m see the[0m[2m same pending[0m[2m job.[0m[2m But in[0m[2m asyncio[0m[2m, only[0m[2m one task[0m[2m runs at[0m[2m a time[0m[2m. If[0m[2m task[0m[2m A starts[0m[2m the for[0m[2m loop and[0m[2m finds a[0m[2m pending job[0m[2m, it[0m[2m will[0m[2m continue until[0m[2m it hits[0m[2m an `[0m[2mawait`.[0m[2m If[0m[2m there's[0m[2m no `[0m[2mawait`[0m[2m between finding[0m[2m and setting[0m[2m,[0m[2m then task[0m[2m B can't[0m[2m inter[0m[2mleave.[0m[2m So removing[0m[2m the `[0m[2mawait asyncio[0m[2m.sleep([0m[2m0.[0m[2m01)`[0m[2m should[0m[2m fix the[0m[2m race condition[0m[2m.
     
